# Intentionally does nothing.
#
# Cloud Shell executes $HOME/.customize_environment automatically at VM boot.
# This file used to hold the superseded VP_TOKEN flow, and it ended with an
# unattended `terraform apply -auto-approve`. That combination is why it is
# empty rather than merely outdated: anyone who copies it to $HOME — which is
# exactly what the "install Terraform yourself" workaround tempts you to do —
# gets an automatic apply against whatever project the shell happens to point
# at, with no pairing code and no confirmation.
#
# Onboarding is `./deploy.sh`, run deliberately, by a person holding a pairing
# code from the VectorPlane dashboard. Nothing here should run on its own.
